    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106-a11">

                <pb facs="0256" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg200"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 23,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I have carefully read, with great
                    pleasure, the letter containing new suggestions upon the matter of
                    fog-signals.</p>
                <p>As regards the signals for indicating the steamer’s helm is going to port, or
                    that it is being put to starboard, I fully agree with; but the one for giving
                    information that it is steady, and likewise you are acting with caution, are
                    liable to be misconstrued and cause great danger.</p>
                <p>I should humbly suggest that a second whistle, of different tone, should be used
                    for giving those signals.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN KELLY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief Officer Steamship
                            Gaelic</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ismay, Imrie</hi> &amp; Co.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
